# docker compose reads this file automatically on `up`. Copy to `.env`
# and fill in the values — `.env` is git-ignored, `.env.example` is not.
#
# ── Base (always required) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Optional. Defaults to the pinned git submodule at vendor/nl-wallet
# (v0.5.0 — must match the wallet app on the test device; v0.5.0 made the
# `x509_san_dns:` client_id prefix mandatory, so a v0.4.1 app cannot talk
# to a v0.5.0 server). Init once with:
#   git submodule update --init vendor/nl-wallet
# NLWALLET_PATH=/absolute/path/to/your/nl-wallet-repo

# ── EUDI profile (only when running with `--profile eudi`) ────────────
#
# The wallet on a phone needs to reach the issuance-server, and the
# issuance-server needs to reach the eudi-adapter. Both need public
# HTTPS URLs. Pick one of three options:
#
#   (a) Own domain / reverse proxy
#       Point two HTTPS hosts at the compose ports and set the URLs
#       below. Skip CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN.
#
#   (b) Cloudflare named tunnel (bundled)
#       Set CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN and start compose with an extra
#       file:
#         COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.cloudflare-tunnel.yml make demo-full
#       The two URLs must match the hostnames you configured in the
#       Cloudflare dashboard. Route the issuance hostname to
#       http://eudi-issuance-server:18001 and the adapter hostname to
#       http://eudi-adapter:4009.
#
#       IMPORTANT: add a final Cloudflare Cache Rule that matches the complete
#       issuance hostname and selects "Bypass cache". Then purge that hostname
#       once. Issuer metadata and request_uri responses are dynamic; caching
#       either breaks the wallet flow and can reuse an issuance session.
#
#   (c) Ad-hoc tunnel (ngrok, cloudflared --url, tailscale funnel, …)
#       Run it yourself, then paste the two URLs below.

# Public HTTPS URL where the wallet reaches the issuance-server.
# Also used by the frontend to build QR codes.
#
# Since nl-wallet v0.5.0 this host is load-bearing for the crypto: the
# issuance-server derives its OpenID4VP client_id from it as
# `x509_san_dns:<host>`, and refuses to start a disclosure use case unless
# EVERY reader certificate in [disclosure_settings.*] carries that host as a
# DNS SAN. Change this host and you must provision new development reader
# certificates before reconciling the sources again.
EUDI_PUBLIC_URL=https://eudi-is.yourdomain.tld/

# Public HTTPS URL where the issuance-server fetches attestations from
# the eudi-adapter.
EUDI_BRI_URL=https://eudi-bri.yourdomain.tld/

# Issuer, reader, and status certificate references come from the activated
# source records rather than separate environment variables. For local use,
# `make provision-development-certificates` creates them explicitly before
# activation. Production uses manually pre-managed certificate material.
# Whether all sources eventually share one GBO set or use separate sets is an
# open design decision tracked in issue #225; the current proof retains the
# existing certificate references per activation.

# Only needed for option (b) above. Cloudflare Zero Trust → Networks →
# Tunnels → your tunnel → Install connector. The eyJ… string from
# `cloudflared service install eyJ…`.
# CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_TOKEN=eyJ...your-token-here...

# ── Host ports (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# All published host ports default to the values below. Override them
# (e.g. +10000) to run a second worktree's stack alongside another one
# without port conflicts. The toestemmingsportaal redirect assumes the
# portal lives one port above the dienstverlener frontend, so keep
# GBO_PORT_TOESTEMMINGSPORTAAL = GBO_PORT_DV_MOCK + 1.
# GBO_PORT_OTEL_GRPC=9317
# GBO_PORT_OTEL_HTTP=9318
# GBO_PORT_JAEGER=9686
# GBO_PORT_LOKI=9310
# GBO_PORT_GRAFANA=9300
# GBO_PORT_OPA=9181
# GBO_PORT_OPA_HEALTH=9180
# GBO_PORT_GRAPHQL=9400
# GBO_PORT_BRP_GRAPHQL=9401
# GBO_PORT_CONSENT_REGISTER=9402
# GBO_PORT_BSNK=9403
# GBO_PORT_SECTOR_PIP=9404
# GBO_PORT_CONSENT_PORTAL_BACKEND=9405
# GBO_PORT_DV_BACKEND=9406
# GBO_PORT_DEV_PORTAL_BACKEND=9407
# GBO_PORT_PDP=9408
# GBO_PORT_EUDI_ADAPTER=9409
# GBO_PORT_BRON_SIDECAR=9411
# GBO_PORT_ADDITIONAL_CLAIMS=9412
# OpenFTV Manager (profile: manager) — management API, the internal API the
# PDP pulls its bundle from, and health.
# Where a BROWSER can reach this stack. Every browser-side link (the
# landing page's flow buttons, Jaeger/Grafana, the FSC controllers) derives
# from it. Leave it on localhost when you demo on the machine itself; set it
# to the host's LAN address when someone else opens the pages, or every link
# will point at *their* localhost.
# GBO_PUBLIC_HOST=localhost
# GBO_PORT_FTV_MANAGER=9280
# GBO_PORT_FTV_MANAGER_INTERNAL=9281
# GBO_PORT_FTV_MANAGER_HEALTH=9282
# GBO_PORT_FTV_MANAGER_UI=9283
# GBO_PORT_KEYCLOAK=9284
# The management interface and its IdP are reached by the BROWSER, so these
# must resolve from wherever you open the page — and must be HTTPS unless
# that is localhost, because the UI's OIDC login uses PKCE and browsers only
# expose Crypto.subtle in a secure context.
# GBO_FTV_MANAGER_URL=https://gbo-ftv-api.example.org
# GBO_FTV_OIDC_AUTHORITY=https://gbo-ftv-auth.example.org/realms/gbo
# Required by `make demo-manager`; configure these as deployment CI/CD variables.
# Only the auditor password is intentionally shared with public demo visitors.
# KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD=
# FTV_MANAGER_AUDITOR_PASSWORD=
# FTV_MANAGER_DEPLOY_PASSWORD=
# Password for the Manager's Postgres (policies, attributes, audit trail).
# FTV_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
# GBO_PORT_BRP_SIDECAR=9413
# GBO_PORT_LANDING=9000
# GBO_PORT_DV_MOCK=9001
# GBO_PORT_TOESTEMMINGSPORTAAL=9002
# GBO_PORT_DEVELOPER_PORTAL=9003
# GBO_PORT_EUDI_ISSUANCE=18001

# ── Landingspagina (optional) ─────────────────────────────────────────
# De landingspagina linkt alleen maar door. De drie frontends volgen
# automatisch de GBO_PORT_* hierboven; de rest wijst standaard naar de
# lokale stack en is hiermee te verleggen naar een gedeployde omgeving.
# FSC_CONTROLLER_BRON_URL=http://localhost:8092
# FSC_CONTROLLER_DVTP_URL=http://localhost:8096
# FSC_CONTROLLER_EUDI_URL=http://localhost:8094
# De wallet-QR op de landingspagina hergebruikt EUDI_PUBLIC_URL en
# EUDI_UL_BASE hierboven; staat EUDI_PUBLIC_URL leeg, dan toont de pagina
# in plaats van de QR waarom er niets te scannen is.
# De client_id in die QR wordt afgeleid uit EUDI_PUBLIC_URL —
# x509_san_dns:<host> — precies zoals de issuance-server hem afleidt.
# Er valt niets te configureren: de server kent geen andere waarde.
# Vrije tekst rechtsonder in de footer, bijvoorbeeld "v0.9.3 · 4f1c2ab".
# VERSION_STRING=

# ── Passwords (required) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Postgres password for the EUDI postgres container (issuance-server +
# migrations). Compose fails loud if unset. Any string works for the
# local demo network.
# EUDI_POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
